{"school":{"dbn":"15K442","name":"M.S. 442 School for Innovation","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"15","district_label":"District 15","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":339,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"500 19 STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11215","phone":"718-965-0390","website":"www.ms442.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/70515","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"M.S. 442 is an award-winning school that has been recognized both city-wide and nationally. Our small school, situated in Windsor Terrace, Brooklyn, follows an inclusion model to support all learners' individual needs. M.S. 442 has been leading the charge in innovation, leadership, and educational excellence. Through our educational use of technology, our students have been provided with blended learning opportunities and individual schedules within an asynchronous model. Our Mastery Based Grading Model allows us to provide personal feedback to students and families. We have our own Fab Lab in partnership with the BEAM Center. This allows us to bring experiential learning to our students with woodworking, circuitry, and electronics. Responsive mentoring between staff and students helps maintain each student's academic, social, and emotional growth, as well as strengthen the home-to-school connection. M.S. 442 also has an extensive offering of activities ranging from student television center to volleyball to SHSAT Prep to musical theater. Students from low-income households, students in temporary housing, and English Language Learners (ELLs) have an admissions priority for 52% of seats at this school.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"F to Prospect Park-15 St","bus":"B61, B67, B68, B69","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Windsor Terrace","latitude":40.656243,"longitude":-73.982559,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_